            <ArticleTitle>[The relation of uric acid metabolism to transferase activity in patients with ischemic heart disease and hypertension].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Blood plasma uric acid and urea content and aspartate aminotransferase activity were studied in 177 patients with ischemic heart disease and essential hypertension. It was established that the blood uric acid level did not depend essentially on the transamination processes in patients with ischemic heart disease but was closely connected with transamination processes and amino acid metabolism in patients with essential hypertension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
